 PLC PROGRAM DOCUMENTATION
  WSN-Based Intelligent Building Automation Using PLC

 1. Overview
The project uses a Siemens S7-1200 PLC to implement intelligent building automation by integrating ESP32-based wireless sensor nodes through Modbus TCP communication.

 2. Hardware and Software
- Siemens S7-1200 PLC (CPU 1215C)
- ESP32 wireless sensor nodes
- Temperature and humidity sensor
- Gas/CO sensor
- Siemens TIA Portal V19
- Ethernet communication
- Modbus TCP protocol

 3. PLC Communication
The Siemens S7-1200 PLC communicates with ESP32 nodes using Modbus TCP. The PLC uses the MB_CLIENT instruction to read sensor data and exchange control information through configured registers.

 4. PLC Programming
The PLC program is developed using ladder logic in Siemens TIA Portal V19. It processes incoming sensor values, evaluates operating conditions and executes the configured automation logic.

 5. System Functions
- Monitoring environmental parameters.
- Reading sensor data from ESP32 nodes.
- Processing temperature and other sensor values.
- Implementing automatic lighting and AC control logic.
- Controlling servo-based actuators.

 6. Communication Configuration
- Protocol: Modbus TCP
- TCP Port: 502
- PLC: Modbus TCP Client
- ESP32: Modbus TCP Server
- Communication medium: Ethernet/Wi-Fi network

 7. Conclusion
The PLC-based automation system demonstrates the integration of wireless sensor networks with industrial control technology. It provides practical experience in PLC programming, Modbus TCP communication, sensor monitoring and intelligent building automation.

  
